          "editorAlias": null,
          "segment": null,
          "value": {
            "blocks": {
              "contentData": [],
              "settingsData": [],
              "expose": [],
              "Layout": {}
            },
            "markup": "\u003Cp class=\u0022govuk-heading-m govuk-body\u0022\u003EAll examples from this point forward use a blue background to show when a \u0027Box\u0027 or \u0027Nested box\u0027 block is used. Aside from the colour they should look the same as the examples that are not inside a \u0027Box\u0027 or \u0027Nested box\u0027.\u003C/p\u003E\n\u003Ch2 class=\u0022govuk-heading-m\u0022\u003EFill the width container\u003C/h2\u003E\n\u003Cp\u003EThe next examples show section cards filling the width container. The first one shows section boxes added at the block grid root, but not using a \u0027Box\u0027.\u003C/p\u003E"
          }
        }
      ]
    },
